  <!-- Technical FAQ Accordion -->
  <section class="section" id="faq">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="badge-tag" data-i18n="faq_badge">Engineering Knowledge Base</div>
        <h2 class="section-title"><span data-i18n="faq_title">Frequently Asked Technical Questions</span></h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle" data-i18n="faq_sub">
          Clear answers on varnish chemistry, ISO contamination standards, and turnaround mobilization.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-accordion">
        <div class="faq-item active">
          <button class="faq-question-btn">
            <span data-i18n="faq_1_q">What causes varnish formation in gas and steam turbine lube systems?</span>
            <svg class="faq-toggle-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-content" data-i18n="faq_1_a">
            Varnish is formed by the thermal and oxidative degradation of turbine lube oils under high operating temperatures, localized micro-dieseling, and spark discharge. Sub-micron soft degradation products polymerize and deposit onto cooler metallic surfaces such as servo-valves, bearings, and heat exchangers, causing sticking and catastrophic trips.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question-btn">
            <span data-i18n="faq_2_q">How fast can Hun Power mobilize emergency skids to Dammam, Jubail, or Yanbu?</span>
            <svg class="faq-toggle-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-content" data-i18n="faq_2_a">
            Our Dammam headquarters maintains dedicated rapid-response skids (VDUs, VRUs, and flushing rigs) on 24/7 standby. We guarantee mobilization to Eastern Province facilities (Dammam, Jubail, Khobar, Ras Tanura) within 2-4 hours, and Western Province (Yanbu, Rabigh, Jeddah) within 12-24 hours.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question-btn">
            <span data-i18n="faq_3_q">What standards are used for hydrostatic hose testing?</span>
            <svg class="faq-toggle-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-content" data-i18n="faq_3_a">
            All hose assemblies fabricated by Hun Power are tested according to ISO 1402 / SAE J517 hydrostatic standards up to 1.5x - 2.0x the maximum working pressure (up to 10,000 PSI) on our computerized test bench, complete with serialized digital test certificates.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question-btn">
            <span data-i18n="faq_4_q">Can varnish removal be executed while the turbine remains on-line?</span>
            <svg class="faq-toggle-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer-content" data-i18n="faq_4_a">
            Yes! Hun Power electrostatic VRU skids operate continuously on-line while the turbine or compressor is generating power. The system extracts both suspended and dissolved varnish precursors, progressively cleaning both the fluid and internal metal reservoir surfaces without shutting down the plant.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

